The release looks at every drained share that waits and leaves each where it was.
A share whose account filled would wait on the spare or spent queue for good;
a drained share that waits has an account not full yet.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a drained share waits with its account full

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -379,7 +379,6 @@ static void release(void)
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < SHARES; i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(SHARES);
         if (shares[i].drained && shares[i].queue != NULL) {
-            share_settle(&shares[i]);
         }
     }
 }
